! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F209B "TESTS OF SIGN AND
! MODIFIER COMBINATIONS" for ADD DOUBLE TO MAGNITUDE, sub-tests
! B14-B16 -- the last three (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.105,
! octal 015543.00-015574.40, where the listing's own exit sequence
! BD,$+1.0 / B,FADM2 / SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW begins). With these,
! F209B is transcribed end to end: B1-B8 and B9-B13 are in the two
! sibling programs and each ends exactly where the next begins.
!
! These are the combinations with BOTH signs negative -- DLN
! accumulator and FPK40 memory operand -- so they close the 4x4 grid
! the routine sweeps:
!
!   B14  D+MGA  acc - mem -   MS+ACS+A+1, N+0
!   B15  D-MG   acc - mem -   MS+ACS+N+1, A+0
!   B16  D-MGA  acc - mem -   MS+ACS+N+A+1
!
! All three expect a negative result and check it with BB, which is
! the sign restore again: D+MG hands back the accumulator's own sign,
! and DLN put a 1 there.
!
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool p.176. The label SAP12 on the first instruction is this
! program's own entry point, not the listing's -- F209B's only printed
! label is FADM2, on B1.
!
! Observed: all three passed on the first run. Like the other
! thirteen they do not reach D+MG's forced zero -- the accumulator is
! at exponent +50 throughout F209B and the operand at +2, so no sum
! can come out negative. F209E, "TEST FORCED ZERO RESULT" (p.107), is
! the routine that does reach it.
!
! Instructions: B, DLN(U), C0011 into the accumulator at offset 20,
! D+MGA(U)/D-MG(U)/D-MGA(U), CT0110 over 48-bit fields at offsets 20
! and 68, BB on a literal bit address, SIC, BRGZ.
! verify_fp_arith_f209b14_16_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --

        SLC, (8)22032.0
FPK21   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031177777777777777767
        SLC, (8)22052.0
FPK37   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031125252525252525240
FPK38   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031052525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22055.0
FPK40   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001052525252525252530

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)15543.0
SAP12   B, $+.32   ! F209B14: MS+ACS+A+1, N+0
        DLN(U), FPK21
        C0011(BU,48), FPK37+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+MGA(U), FPK40
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK21+.12, 20   ! test low order result fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK21+.12, 68   ! test high order result fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BB, 10.04, $+2.0   ! test the accumulator sign bit: expect -
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F209B15: MS+ACS+N+1, A+0
        DLN(U), FPK21
        C0011(BU,48), FPK37+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D-MG(U), FPK40
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK21+.12, 20   ! test low order result fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK21+.12, 68   ! test high order result fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BB, 10.04, $+2.0   ! test the accumulator sign bit: expect -
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F209B16: MS+ACS+N+A+1
        DLN(U), FPK38
        C0011(BU,48), FPK37+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D-MGA(U), FPK40
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK40+.12, 20   ! test low order result fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK40+.12, 68   ! test high order result fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BB, 10.04, $+2.0   ! test the accumulator sign bit: expect -
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                 ! 015574.40: F209B exits here
        END, SAP12
